---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility | CenTex Press"
  description="How CenTex Press builds for accessibility, and how to report a barrier or request an accessible alternative."
>
<SiteHeader />
<main id="main" class="container legal-page">
  <header class="legal-head">
    <h1>Accessibility at CenTex Press</h1>
    <p class="legal-dates">Effective Date: September 17, 2026 · Last Updated: September 17, 2026</p>
  </header>

  <div class="legal-body">
    <h2>News should be accessible to everyone.</h2>
    <p>CenTex Press believes everyone in our community should be able to access local news, public information and the documents behind our reporting.</p>
    <p>Disability should not be a barrier to knowing what your local government is doing, understanding an issue affecting your family, reading a community story or participating in the public conversation.</p>
    <p>Accessibility is therefore part of how we are building CenTex Press, not something we intend to add later.</p>

    <h2>Our Accessibility Goal</h2>
    <p>CenTex Press aims to conform to the <strong>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2, Level AA</strong>, the international accessibility standard published by the World Wide Web Consortium.</p>
    <p>These guidelines are designed to make websites more accessible to people with a wide range of disabilities and accessibility needs.</p>
    <p>Our goal is for CenTex Press to be:</p>
    <p class="emphasis-line">Perceivable. Operable. Understandable. Robust.</p>
    <p>And, just as importantly:</p>
    <p class="emphasis-line">Readable by real people using real devices.</p>

    <h2>How We Build for Accessibility</h2>
    <p>CenTex Press is being designed with accessibility built into the website itself.</p>
    <p>That includes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Semantic HTML and logical heading structures</li>
      <li>Keyboard-accessible navigation</li>
      <li>Visible keyboard focus indicators</li>
      <li>Skip-to-content navigation</li>
      <li>Alternative text for meaningful images</li>
      <li>Sufficient contrast between text and backgrounds</li>
      <li>Text that can be enlarged without losing content or functionality</li>
      <li>Responsive layouts for phones, tablets and computers</li>
      <li>Clearly labeled links and buttons</li>
      <li>Accessible form labels and instructions</li>
      <li>Screen-reader-friendly page structure</li>
      <li>Reduced-motion support for readers who request it through their device or browser</li>
      <li>Captions, transcripts or text alternatives when practical for multimedia content</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not believe an accessibility widget should be a substitute for building an accessible website.</p>

    <h2>Public Documents and The Receipts</h2>
    <p>CenTex Press publishes and links to government records through <strong><a href="/receipts">The Receipts</a></strong>.</p>
    <p>These may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Budgets</li>
      <li>Agendas</li>
      <li>Ordinances</li>
      <li>Contracts</li>
      <li>Audits</li>
      <li>Reports</li>
      <li>Public records</li>
      <li>Presentations</li>
      <li>Scanned government documents</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Some of these documents were created by third parties or government agencies and may not have been designed for accessibility.</p>
    <p>Older PDFs and scanned documents can be especially difficult for screen readers because they may contain images of text rather than machine-readable text.</p>
    <p>When practical, CenTex Press will provide context, descriptions or accessible information alongside important source documents.</p>

    <h2>Images</h2>
    <p>Images that communicate meaningful information should include appropriate alternative text or accompanying descriptions.</p>
    <p>Purely decorative images should be identified so assistive technologies can skip them.</p>
    <p>For charts, graphics and data visualizations, our goal is to communicate important information in text as well as visually.</p>

    <h2>Video and Audio</h2>
    <p>When CenTex Press publishes original video or audio, we will work toward providing captions, transcripts or another appropriate text alternative.</p>
    <p>Embedded videos and other content hosted by outside platforms may be subject to the accessibility practices of those providers.</p>

    <h2>Advertising and External Content</h2>
    <p>CenTex Press may display advertisements and link to or embed information provided by third parties.</p>
    <p>We cannot completely control the accessibility of websites, advertising platforms, social-media services, embedded videos or other services operated by outside organizations.</p>
    <p>Where practical, we will favor technology and partners that support accessible experiences.</p>

    <h2>Español</h2>
    <p>Accessibility also means making information understandable to the communities we serve.</p>
    <p>CenTex Press is being designed to support journalism in both <strong>English and Spanish</strong>.</p>
    <p>Language availability may vary by story, and we will identify translated content when available.</p>

    <h2>If You Encounter a Barrier</h2>
    <p>We want to know.</p>
    <p>If something on CenTex Press prevents you from accessing information, reading an article, navigating the website, submitting information or using one of our features, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>
    <p>It helps if you can tell us:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which page caused the problem</li>
      <li>What you were trying to do</li>
      <li>What went wrong</li>
      <li>What device or browser you were using, if known</li>
      <li>What assistive technology you were using, if applicable</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You do not need to understand accessibility terminology to report a problem.</p>
    <p>Simply tell us what happened.</p>

    <h2>Request an Accessible Alternative</h2>
    <p>If you cannot access a CenTex Press article, document, image, video or other material because of an accessibility barrier, <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>
    <p>When reasonably possible, we will work with you to provide the information in another accessible format.</p>
    <p>That could include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A text version of information</li>
      <li>A description of an image or graphic</li>
      <li>Help locating information within a document</li>
      <li>A transcript or written summary</li>
      <li>Another reasonable accessible format</li>
    </ul>
    <p>There is no charge for requesting an accessible alternative.</p>

    <h2>Accessibility Is Ongoing</h2>
    <p>CenTex Press is a growing newsroom, and the website will continue to change.</p>
    <p>New stories, documents, advertisements, multimedia, community submissions and technology will create new accessibility challenges.</p>
    <p>We will continue improving the site as we find problems and as accessibility standards and technology evolve.</p>
    <p>If we get something wrong, tell us.</p>
    <p>We would rather know about the problem and work to fix it than pretend every part of the website will always be perfect.</p>

    <h2>Contact CenTex Press</h2>
    <p>For an accessibility question, request or problem, reach us through our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.</p>
    <p><strong>CenTex Press</strong><br />Central Texas, United States</p>

    <div class="principle">
      <p class="principle-line">Local news is public information. Everyone should be able to reach it.</p>
      <p class="principle-brand"><strong>CenTex Press</strong><br /><em>Different voices. One community.</em></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
<SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.legal-page{padding-block:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,5rem);max-width:800px}
.legal-head{border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink);padding-bottom:1.5rem;margin-bottom:2rem}
.legal-head h1{font:900 clamp(2.2rem,5.5vw,3.6rem)/.98 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:0 0 .6rem}
.legal-dates{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;margin:0}
.legal-body p,.legal-body li{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted)}
.legal-body p{margin:0 0 1.1rem;max-width:70ch}
.legal-body ul{margin:0 0 1.1rem;padding-left:1.4rem;max-width:70ch}
.legal-body li{margin-bottom:.3rem}
.legal-body strong{color:var(--ink)}
.legal-body a{color:var(--ink);font-weight:800;text-underline-offset:4px}
.legal-body h2{font:800 clamp(1.25rem,2.6vw,1.6rem)/1.15 Georgia,serif;color:var(--ink);margin:2.25rem 0 1rem}
.legal-body .emphasis-line{font-weight:800;color:var(--ink);font-size:1.05rem}
.principle{margin-top:2.5rem;padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface)}
.principle-line{font-weight:800;color:var(--ink);font-size:1.1rem;margin-bottom:1rem}
.principle-brand{margin:0;color:var(--muted)}
.principle-brand strong{color:var(--ink)}
</style>
